<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">04042026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Iran's air defenses have downed a US F-fifteen-E Strike Eagle over central Iran — the first American manned aircraft lost in thirty-five days of war.</s> <s>One crew member's been rescued, but the second is still missing as US helicopters search deep inside hostile territory.</s> <s>Tehran is pressing its advantage, with the military threatening larger strikes on Tel Aviv, while former foreign minister Zarif argues in Foreign Affairs that Iran should declare victory now and negotiate before each infrastructure strike erodes what leverage remains.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Trump posted on Truth Social that the US can, quote, take the oil and make a fortune — making the seizure of Iran's resources his explicit war aim.</s> <s>Pillage of sovereign natural resources is prohibited under the Fourth Geneva Convention, a legal line no American president has publicly crossed.</s> <s>His administration simultaneously requested one-point-five trillion dollars for defense in twenty twenty-seven, a forty percent increase and the sharpest since World War Two.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Iranian drone strikes hit Kuwait's Mina al-Ahmadi refinery and a desalination plant supplying drinking water to the capital overnight.</s> <s>Britain deployed its Rapid Sentry counter-drone system within hours — the UK's first active military deployment in Kuwait in years.</s> <s>Tehran has warned Gulf states hosting American bases to expel US forces or face strikes alongside Israeli and American energy targets.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's fuel prices jumped forty-three percent, and the country's trade federation has declared an economic emergency as textile mills and small factories face shutdown.</s> <s>Four provinces are pooling two hundred billion rupees to subsidize motorcyclists, farmers, and truckers, while Islamabad simultaneously repays three-point-five billion dollars to Abu Dhabi — cutting central bank reserves eighteen percent.</s> <s>Analysts warn the outflow will pressure the rupee and jeopardize IMF reserve requirements at exactly the moment Pakistan can least afford it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>World food prices rose two-point-four percent in March, the UN Food and Agriculture Organization reported, driven by war-time energy costs rippling through global supply chains.</s> <s>Sugar climbed seven percent and vegetable oil over five, as fuel and fertilizer costs hit producers hardest in the Global South.</s> <s>FAO's chief economist warns that farmers priced out of planting will cut global yields through twenty twenty-seven — a hunger timeline, not just an inflation story.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>US funding cuts have halted Zimbabwe's rollout of lenacapavir, a breakthrough HIV drug that requires just one injection every six months instead of daily pills.</s> <s>If supply gaps persist, interrupted treatment won't just fail patients — it risks creating drug-resistant HIV strains that spread far beyond Zimbabwe's borders.</s> <s>What was a budget line in Washington is now a ticking biological clock in Harare.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Archaeologists have catalogued five hundred and sixty-five dice from forty-five Native American sites spanning twelve thousand years, predating Bronze Age Mesopotamia's earliest known dice by six millennia.</s> <s>These aren't random game pieces — they show structured, rule-based play suggesting an intuitive grasp of probability the Old World record can't match.</s> <s>A new paper in American Antiquity argues the history of mathematics must now trace probability's origins to Ice Age North America.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Artemis Two crew have photographed the whole Earth from lunar distance — the first time humans have been far enough from home to see it entire since nineteen seventy-two.</s> <s>After fifty-four years, people are orbiting the Moon again, a milestone that felt like fiction just a decade ago.</s> <s>Artemis Three, the crewed landing, still awaits a date — God willing, it won't take another fifty-four years.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Fifteen patients at Vanderbilt University Medical Center refused life-saving blood transfusions because the blood came from COVID-vaccinated donors.</s> <s>Most were children whose families cited conspiracy theories; two surgeries were delayed and one patient went into shock.</s> <s>US blood donations fell thirty-five percent in January, and hospitals report that directed requests for unvaccinated blood are depleting reserves nationwide.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A randomized controlled trial in ninety-eight people, published in Nature, found that plant polyphenols reduced immune inflammation caused by microplastics over twenty-eight days.</s> <s>This isn't a mouse study — it's the first human evidence that a dietary intervention can counter the immune disruption microplastics cause in our blood.</s> <s>Researchers identified two biological mediators, pointing toward polyphenols as a genuine clinical candidate rather than a wellness trend.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Kerala became the first Indian state to designate an official state microbe, anchoring a new microbiome research hub aimed at sustainable agriculture and gut health.</s> <s>The hub plans to convert laboratory findings directly into farming and health policy — a rare effort to bridge science and governance at the state level.</s> <s>Whether it produces real change or remains a symbolic first will depend on funding and political will.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A technical analysis from Berlin argues that existing solar panels and battery storage can already meet global energy demand — no new breakthroughs required.</s> <s>The <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme> blockade and hundred-and-fifteen-dollar oil now pressure-test every government still subsidizing fossil fuels.</s> <s>It's no longer about whether renewables can replace hydrocarbons — it's about how fast politics will allow it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Google's quantum computing team showed it can derive a Bitcoin wallet's private key from its public key in nine minutes — just under Bitcoin's ten-minute transaction window.</s> <s>The threat isn't to mining but to ownership: six-point-nine million Bitcoin have permanently exposed public keys, making them vulnerable once quantum hardware scales.</s> <s>Unlike Ethereum, Bitcoin has no post-quantum migration plan, and its governance moves too slowly to build one before the threat arrives.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A University of Pennsylvania study of nearly fourteen hundred people found that seventy-three percent accepted wrong answers from AI without question.</s> <s>Fluent, confident AI outputs suppress the metacognitive signals that normally trigger deliberate reasoning — the internal alarm that says something's off simply doesn't fire.</s> <s>Time pressure made correction rates twelve points worse, while financial incentives barely helped at all.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
